        "payload": "tree 07c48d5bcf0bf1dae475c14ed49bd131da1d7836\nparent 67f76cbebc78ecf941a8e1bf73e6b96fa00b818b\nauthor Alex Gleason <alex@alexgleason.me> 1780250603 +0200\ncommitter Alex Gleason <alex@alexgleason.me> 1780250603 +0200\n\nAuto-select unambiguous recipients in Send picker\n\nWhen the recipient input resolves to a single unambiguous recipient,\ncreate the chip immediately instead of showing a one-item dropdown:\n\n- a bare npub or nprofile resolves to a Nostr account chip;\n- a bare address or single-endpoint bitcoin: URI creates the chip.\n\nDual-endpoint bitcoin: URIs (both an on-chain address and an sp= silent\npayment address) still surface both rows so the user picks the\nprivacy/compatibility trade-off, and nip05 identifiers stay in the\ndropdown because their resolution is asynchronous.\n\nBare hex pubkeys are no longer accepted — the format is ambiguous and\nnot user-facing.\n",
